-- Rifts World Book 33: Northern Gun One, three robots (printed 126-141): Gunbot, Gunwolf, Grizzly
-- 3 vehicle rows, with 54 locations and 27 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~287-northern-gun-1-robots-c.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('ng-v47-gunbot', 'Gunbot Combat Robot', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Three: a pilot and two gunners, in two separate cockpits', NULL, 'Running 75 mph (120 km); 105 mph (168 km) power jumping and bounding at speed; leaps 30 ft (9.1 m) high or across unaided, 50 ft (15.2 m) high and up to 100 ft (30.5 m) across with the jets, either doubled at 50 mph (80 km) or faster', 'Not possible', 'Cannot swim; walks the lake or sea bed at 30 mph (48 km); maximum depth 2,000 ft (610 m)', 'Height 18 ft 10 in (5.8 m); width 12 ft (3.6 m) at the hips, the turret body 9 ft (2.7 m) launcher to launcher and 11 ft (3.3 m) with the shields out; length 18 ft (5.5 m)', '12, plus 3.2 fully loaded with ammunition and missiles', 390, 1, NULL, 21000000, '31 million credits nuclear, 24 million Solid Oxide Fuel Cell, 21 million electric battery; good availability; the lowest is stored.', 'Model Type: NG-V47 Gunbot Light Artillery (headed Gunbot Robot-Killer on p.126; the name here is the book''s Alphabetical List of NG Combat Robots, p.100). Class: Infantry Assault and Support Robot. An armless, low-slung two-legged gun platform built to hunt bigger robots, tanks and armored monsters such as Fury Beetles, dinosaurs and dragons; salespeople and mercenaries call it a tank-killer and a dragon slayer. It carries more guns than armor and survives by moving: jets in the calves and three in the back give it huge assisted leaps, and a dozen small thrusters keep it balanced. The favored tactic is to wait in cover, open up from ambush with every gun at once, then bound away to a new position or close for the kill; it also serves as a perimeter turret, crouched behind an open-topped wall it can jump out of. Its weakness is light armor, since NG lacks the alloys and avionics of the CS and Triax. Market acceptance has been slow, but NG uses it in its own defenses. Motion defense: while it moves, all attackers are -1 to strike, and -2 more on Called Shots. The pilot in the upper cockpit moves it; in the lower cockpit one gunner works the nose guns and the other the missiles and grenade cannon; the whole upper body turns like a tank turret to aim the nose guns. Robot P.S. 35. Cargo: one small locker, room for a rifle and a pistol, a survival kit, some personal effects and 10 gallons (37.9 liters) of water. Power: nuclear, 15 year average life; fuel cell and battery versions last 5.6 years. Hand to hand per Light Ground Robot Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.353); it has no arms, so no punch, power punch or parry: nose barrel swat 2D4 M.D.; kick 2D8+4 M.D.; leap kick 4D8+8 M.D. (two attacks); jet-boosted power leap kick 1D4x10+12 M.D. (three attacks, needs a running start); stomp 2D4 M.D. against targets 6 ft (1.8 m) or shorter; leaping stomp 1D6x10+12 M.D. (three attacks, -2 to strike, landing on the target); body block or ram 2D6 M.D., 01-66% to knock down a foe its size or smaller (+1D6 M.D. and +1D6% at top speed), the fallen losing initiative and one attack. Sensors: the standard NG robot features.', 'Rifts World Book 33: Northern Gun One p.126-129'),
  ('ng-v61-gunwolf', 'Gunwolf Combat Robot', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Two: a pilot and a copilot/communications engineer, both in the chest', NULL, 'Running 60 mph (96 km); leaps only 10 ft (3 m) high and 18 ft (5.5 m) across with a running start', 'Not applicable', 'Not built for water; walks the bottom at up to 25 mph (40 km); maximum depth 1,200 ft (366 m)', 'Height 26 ft (7.9 m); width 20 ft (6 m) at the shoulders; length 14 ft (4.2 m)', '30, fully loaded', 480, 1, NULL, 31000000, '38 million credits nuclear, 34 million Solid Oxide Fuel Cell, 31 million electric battery; the lowest is stored.', 'Model Type: NG-V61 Gunwolf. Class: Anti-Monster and Infantry Combat Robot. NG''s answer to a gap in its line: a heavy machine meant to stand against hordes of demons and monsters, Xiticix swarms and giant horrors like dragons, while still able to fight robots, power armor and ordinary troops. It wears a stylized wolf''s head with silver-plated teeth and crushing jaws, and silver-plated claws on both hands that also climb, dig and tear through defenses. Most of its guns are rail guns firing conventional, silver-coated or wooden rounds ringed with silver, backed by an ion cannon, eye lasers, plasma mini-missiles and a flamethrower in the mouth. Its crews like to bait a monster into charging, then hold it with jaws or claws while every gun fires at point-blank range. Out on the market only a year, it sells to mercenaries, bounty and monster hunters and to city-states troubled by monsters, and NG fields it in its own reserve and on border patrols: a patrol is 1D4+2 Gunwolves with two fast small robots or 3-4 power armor troops; a squad of 8-10 (the Northern Wolves) and a platoon of 14-20 (a Wolf Pack) bring 2-4 other robots and 2-8 power armor. Two weaknesses: once the ammunition is spent it has only melee and energy weapons, which many supernatural foes shrug off, and swarms can overwhelm it; and its bulk and spiky profile make it a loud, clumsy woodland hunter that snags on every branch, heard a mile (1.6 km) away. The crew sits in the chest, not the head. Robot P.S. 40. Cargo: lockers on each thigh and the pelvis, two small ones on the knees and a larger one in the back unit, each with 50 M.D.C. Power: nuclear, 20 year average life; fuel cell and battery versions too. Hand to hand per Heavy Ground Robot Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352): restrained punch 1D4 M.D.; punch 2D6 M.D.; head butt 2D4 M.D.; claw strike or rake 3D6+4 M.D.; power claw strike 6D6+8 M.D. (two attacks); power claw rip with both hands at once 1D6x10 M.D. (three attacks, and it cannot parry the next attack); kick 3D6 M.D.; stomp 1D6 M.D.; running ram 3D6 M.D., two attacks, 70% to knock down a foe of its size, smaller or up to 20% larger and 45% against one up to twice its size, the fallen losing initiative and two attacks. Its claws cannot work giant-sized guns; giant melee weapons are -1 to strike, parry and disarm. Sensors beyond the NG standard: thermal imager (2,000 ft/610 m), infrared and ultraviolet optics, infrared searchlights on an arm behind the left shoulder that reaches out 6 ft (1.8 m) more (500 ft/152 m), and cameras in the eye sockets, forearms, chest cluster, missile launchers and back (4,000 ft/1,219 m, telescopic and macro, with image and video transmission).', 'Rifts World Book 33: Northern Gun One p.129-134'),
  ('ng-v67-grizzly', 'Grizzly Combat Robot', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Two: a pilot in the chest and a copilot/gunner in the head', NULL, 'Running 35 mph (56 km); leaping not possible; cannot manage slopes steeper than 40 degrees', 'Not possible', 'Cannot swim; walks the lake bed at up to 10 mph (16 km); maximum depth 2,000 ft (610 m)', 'Height 32.8 ft (10 m); width 22.4 ft (6.8 m); length 19.7 ft (6 m)', '43, fully loaded', 700, 1, NULL, 48000000, '48 million credits, nuclear only: the ion weapons draw too much for any other power supply. Out of stock since release; the secondary market charges 50% to 200% more.', 'Model Type: NG-V67 Grizzly. Class: Anti-Armor, Anti-Monster and Infantry Artillery Combat Robot. A huge, slow walking gun platform for supporting troops in the field, holding ground as a mobile bunker and guard tower, defending towns, and shredding Xiticix swarms, monsters, demons and armor; both monster-slayer and tank-killer, like the Gunwolf. Released six months ago and sold out ever since. It is among the most heavily armored machines NG has sold openly, and executives argued over whether arming independents and mercenaries would anger the Coalition; the CS has said nothing. Too big for forest, deep mud or mountains, it does well in desert, prairie, city streets and rubble, wades strong rivers, walks lake and coastal floors, and pairs well with the Beachmaster for beach landings. Extra exterior plates cover its shoulders, arms, hands and legs, and the limbs beneath cannot be hurt until a plate is gone. It turns 180 degrees at the waist; the top turret turns 360 and the shoulder laser can fire ahead, up or behind while the rest engage elsewhere. Many weapons are modular, swapped by an Operator or NG Certified Mechanic in 20-40 minutes (forearm weapons 6-10 minutes with the right gear, double without); the alternates are listed after the standard weapons, and the right forearm can also take an NG-SH-7 searchlight pair (25,000 credits), a 3D camera and holographic projector with facial recognition (120,000) or a long-range communications and data relay (75,000) instead of a gun. Crews are urged to wear environmental armor that takes a jet pack, and two compartments hold one each, because an overrun Grizzly is hard to get out of; a destruct mechanism can fry its insides. Robot P.S. 40. Cargo: each cockpit stows a jet pack, backpack, rifle, canteens and a small bag. Power: nuclear, 20 year average life. Hand to hand per Heavy Ground Robot Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352), but only +1 to parry and dodge for its size: restrained punch 1D4+1 M.D.; punch 2D6+3 M.D.; power punch 4D6+6 M.D. (two attacks), +1D6 M.D. from the knuckle-spiked hand, usually the left; stomp 2D4 M.D.; running ram standard; no head butt, kick or leap kick. Its big armored hands cannot work most giant-sized guns, but use giant melee weapons without penalty. Sensors beyond the NG standard: thermal imager (2,000 ft/610 m), infrared and ultraviolet optics, an extending infrared searchlight arm behind the left shoulder (500 ft/152 m), cameras in the chest, weapon arms and thighs (4,000 ft/1,219 m, x10 magnification, 100 mile/160 km transmission, 10,000 hours stored), and a belly winch, hook and tow line between the chest guns.', 'Rifts World Book 33: Northern Gun One p.134-141');

